title: Coalition Affairs
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; coalition_affairs_timer = 5
view-if: spd_in_government = 1 and coalition_dissent >= 1 and coalition_affairs_timer = 0 and (in_grand_coalition or in_weimar_coalition or in_popular_front)
card-image: img/muller_cabinet.jpg
#subtitle: There is dissent within our coalition.

= Coalition Affairs

Our coalition is in trouble. The right-leaning members of the [? if in_german_coalition: GDVP ?][? if in_grand_coalition: Landbund and CSP ?] are constantly criticizing us for our policies, and are threatening to call a vote of no confidence to collapse this government.

How do we reduce tensions with the coalition?

- @promise_cuts: Agree to the bourgeois plans to cut welfare.
- @resources: Use our party resources to support our allies.
- @unity_convince: Can we convince our partners to adopt our economic plan?
- @unity_enact: Can we enact the Unity Plan?
- @bring_down: Instead, we will bring down the government with a no-confidence vote, and call for new elections.
- @no_change: Take none of these actions.
- @easy_discard


@promise_cuts
on-arrival: workers_sdapo -= 5; unemployed_sdapo -= 6; workers_kpo += 3; workers_rspo += 2 if rspo_consolidated == 1; unemployed_kpo += 2; unemployed_rspo += 1 if rspo_consolidated == 1; workers_kpo += 2 if rspo_consolidated != 1; unemployed_kpo += 1 if rspo_consolidated != 1; unemployed_dnsap += 3; left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 5; welfare -= 1; budget += 1; coalition_dissent = 0

Fine. By cutting welfare, we have reduced dissent within the coalition.

@resources
subtitle: -2 resources
view-if: historical_mode = 0
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources (need 2).
choose-if: resources >= 2
on-arrival: resources -= 2; coalition_dissent -= 1

By transferring campaign funds to our coalition partners, we can make our policies more acceptable to them. Some would call this corruption, but perhaps it is necessary to save democracy.

@unity_convince
subtitle: A shared programme could help combat extremism, but may be hard to accomplish...
view-if: moderate_plan_adopted == 1 and unity_plan_adopted != 1 and unity_rejected != 1
choose-if: unity_willingness == 1
unavailable-subtitle: Our partners are not willing to be convinced of the plan's merits.
on-arrival: csp_relation -= 2
go-to: unity_plan

@unity_enact
view-if: unity_plan_adopted == 1 and sdapo_in_government == 1 and economic_minister_party != "SDAPO" and finance_minister_party != "SDAPO"
go-to: unity_enacting

@no_change

No. We will not do this.

@bring_down
subtitle: Bring down this government before our opponents do.
on-arrival: sdapo_in_government = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_german_coalition = 0; chancellor = "Seipel"; chancellor_party = "CSP"; next_election_time = time + 3 if next_election_time > time+3; next_election_month = month + 3 if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year = year if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12; sdapo_toleration = 0; left_strength += 8; new_middle_sdapo -= 3; rural_sdapo -= 3; old_middle_sdapo -= 3; catholics_sdapo -= 3; reformist_dissent += 5

We have called for a vote of no confidence in ourselves, and have brought down this government. Chancellor [+ chancellor +] currently rules as acting chancellor.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

